You’re given a valid parentheses string s.
A primitive parentheses string is one that cannot be split into two non-empty valid parentheses strings.

👉 Your task: Remove the outermost parentheses of every primitive substring and return the result.

s = "(()())(())"
break into primitive 
(()())   (())

remove parenthessi 
()()     ()

output
"()()()"

class Solution {
    public String removeOuterParentheses(String s) {
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
        int depth = 0;

        for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (ch == '(') {
                if (depth > 0) result.append(ch);
                depth++;
            } else {
                depth--;
                if (depth > 0) result.append(ch);
            }
        }

        return result.toString();
    }
}

⏱️ Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(n) (for result)
